Upstream-to-vendor delta:
- src/proto/h1/io.rs: limit ReadBuf to Hyper's positive computed next budget.
  Retain the original full spare slice when next == 0, because the public
  client read_buf_exact_size(Some(0)) must still consume available input,
  never report a false EOF. Two read_buffer_regression tests from reviewed
  predecessor 6c8d7e57c4a5dc01d1330d6051076236989f7d44 cover deterministic
  excess spare capacity and exact-zero client progress.
- src/proto/h1/io.rs and src/proto/h1/conn.rs (#292): after Hyper's
  partial-read terminator fast path has deferred parsing, an actual EOF or the
  raw-head byte limit gets one full bounded parse before terminal
  classification. This makes earlier malformed bytes reject consistently
  across whole and fragmented reads, keeps a genuinely incomplete maximum-size
  head at `TooLarge`, and keeps a smaller well-formed incomplete head at
  `IncompleteMessage`. The EOF reparse does not poll the transport again. The
  focused connection regression uses deterministic in-memory I/O and counts
  exact EOF polls.
- src/proto/h1/io.rs and src/proto/h1/conn.rs (#292): HTTP/2 prior-knowledge
  recognition requires the exact raw position-zero preface. The old parse-error
  path discarded leading CR/LF before checking the preface, so a prefixed input
  could be classified as HTTP/2 when read whole but malformed HTTP/1 when the
  leading byte arrived separately. The focused connection regression retains
  the raw-position rule; exact position-zero preface behavior is unchanged.
- src/proto/h1/role.rs (#292): reject a raw request-target `#` before conversion
  to `http::Uri`, which otherwise omits the fragment from the value presented
  to strict policy. The server-only regression retains this parser rejection;
  response/client parsing is unchanged.
- src/proto/h1/role.rs (#289): preserve each numerically identical request
  Content-Length field in the parsed HeaderMap so the existing strict
  MultipleContentLengths application policy can reject it. Decoder length
  selection is unchanged; conflicting/invalid lengths still fail at Hyper.
  Transfer-Encoding precedence, Content-Length removal with TE, and disabled
  connection reuse for CL+TE are unchanged. Three content_length_regression
  tests check field preservation, invalid/conflicting lengths and TE precedence;
  CI also retains upstream test_decoder_request. No client/response parser change.
- Cargo.toml: an empty [workspace] isolates the upstream unit-test workspace.
  It does not add Hyper to Eidolon's members or change production features.
- .gitignore: keep the packaged Cargo.toml.orig despite the root *.orig rule
  and exclude build output from the standalone test workspace.
